The cart service is in place for story 03-app. It keeps its own `cart_db`, checks sellability and price with the catalog over HTTP, and exposes Swagger at `/docs`.

- `POST /cart` creates a cart.
- `POST /cart/{cart_id}/items` snapshots the catalog price and refuses an unsellable product with a reason.
- `PATCH /cart/{cart_id}/items/{product_id}` recomputes the total and drops a line when the quantity is zero.
- `GET` and `DELETE` read or remove that cart only.

`cart/tests`: 9 passed. `catalog/tests`: 6 passed. `identity/tests` still fails to collect because `email-validator` is not installed; that failure is unchanged.

